# ─── Rust ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed. Cartograph ships a binary; a reproducible build of
# a released version matters more than testing against fresh dependency
# versions, and CI can update it deliberately.

# ─── Benchmarks and profiling ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Criterion writes reports and baselines into target/, which is already
# ignored. These cover profiling output written elsewhere.
*.profraw
perf.data*
*.trace
flamegraph.svg

# ─── Analysis output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The local graph database Cartograph writes when analysing a repository.
# It contains derived information about the user's source and must never be
# committed (RULE 011).
.cartograph/
*.cartograph.redb

# ─── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credentials live in the OS keychain, never in files (RULE 014). These
# patterns are a backstop, not the mechanism.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials.json

# ─── Python (vendored AgentOS toolchain only) ──────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# ─── Node (desktop application, from M11) ──────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# The Tauri shell is its own cargo workspace (ADR-0016), so the root-anchored
# /target/ rule above does not reach it.
desktop/src-tauri/target/
# tauri-build regenerates the permission schemas on every build.
desktop/src-tauri/gen/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── macOS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store

# AppleDouble sidecar files. The repository lives on an exFAT volume, which
# has no native extended-attribute support, so macOS materialises xattrs as
# `._name` files next to every file it touches — including inside .git, where
# they make Git print "non-monotonic index" errors. `make clean-sidecars`
# removes them. See docs/development/external-storage.md.
._*
.AppleDouble
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Generated benchmark fixture: ~2 MB of derived JSON, regenerated with
# `cargo test -p cartograph-desktop --test fixture_10k -- --ignored`.
desktop/public/scene-10k.json
desktop/bench-result.json

# Generated by the blast CLI test suite.
crates/cartograph-cli/tests/fixtures/blast/
